 "method": "For each frame, up to 9 nights in the window are fetched from the GIBS WMS at about 500 m and combined with a per-pixel median. Display gray levels are mapped back to radiance bins with the layer's GIBS colormap (nW/(cm^2 sr), saturating at 38.2), summed inside fixed city boxes, and compared with the region's baseline frame. Robustness checks per frame: above_background_vs_baseline_pct subtracts the frame-wide median radiance before summing; single_night_range_vs_baseline_pct gives the spread of the individual nights; gray_sum_vs_baseline_pct sums raw display gray levels (dominated by the dark background). brightness_vs_baseline_pct is an approximate brightness change from display imagery, not a calibrated radiance analysis.",
 "metric_label": "Approximate brightness change from display imagery",
